Description: Cursor shape (DECSCUSR, CSI Ps SP q) support
 Stock mosh 1.4.0 swallows "ESC [ Ps SP q", so an application's cursor
 style (e.g. nvim's bar cursor in INSERT mode) never reaches the local
 terminal.  This parses DECSCUSR into DrawState::cursor_shape on the
 server's terminal emulator, carries it through the state sync (it is
 part of DrawState::operator==, so a shape-only change is a real diff),
 and re-emits it from Display::new_frame on the client.  Both
 mosh-server and mosh-client need the patch.
 .
 Based on the unmerged upstream PR mobile-shell/mosh#1355 "Cursor shape
 support" by dabeibao (head 4ead8960e399d2e8861f719185de739bab281ad1),
 rebased by hand onto the 1.4.0 release, with these changes:
  - initial/default shape is 0 ("terminal default"), not -1.  With -1, a
    full reset (RIS) after a shape was set went back to -1 and the client
    never told the terminal, leaving e.g. a bar cursor behind.  Now any
    change, including back to 0, is sent as ESC [ Ps SP q.
  - on a full repaint (initialized == false: first frame, resume after
    Ctrl-^ Ctrl-Z, Ctrl-L repaint) a non-default shape is re-sent; the
    PR only sent it on change, so a resumed client lost the shape.
  - Display::close() takes the last drawn frame and emits ESC [ 0 SP q
    when the shape is not the default, so the cursor is restored when
    mosh exits or is suspended.  Nothing is sent if no shape was set.
  - the new emulation-cursor-shape.test is added to src/tests/Makefile.am
    (the PR added the file but never ran it), and fixed: it now clears
    the screen first like the other emulation tests (without that the
    mosh and direct captures differ by a blank line; it failed even
    with the escapes replaced by plain text), and a post hook checks
    the tmux log that mosh-client really sent ESC [ 1..6 SP q, and
    ESC [ 0 SP q on exit.
 Used by the K4510 project (github.com/mlongval/k4510): nvim -> tmux ->
 mosh-server (Ubuntu noble) -> mosh-client (K4510x, Debian trixie) ->
 JIM, which implements DECSCUSR.
Origin: other, https://github.com/mobile-shell/mosh/pull/1355
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-09
